cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "hb1d-cycles: exact search for heavy-ball cycles on one-dimensional functions at tunings outside the augmented root-of-unity region"
abstract: >-
  Exact (rational Farkas certificates, interval arithmetic) search for heavy-ball cycles on one-dimensional L-smooth
  mu-strongly convex functions at tunings outside the augmented root-of-unity region Omega_aug of Fotopoulos,
  Helcig, Deck and Alsbach, and in the fan tongues of Pasechnyuk-Vilensky. No counterexample to the one-dimensional
  consequence of the conjecture Omega_aug = Omega_cyc^(2) is found: at Pasechnyuk-Vilensky's Proposition 9.4 tuning
  (kappa = 100) there is no 1D cycle of any length K <= 25, and at two rational tunings found here in the 2/7 and
  2/9 fan tongues, which have cycles in R^4, there is no 1D cycle of length K <= 14 (K <= 16 at the second). Every
  exclusion at the named tunings, and every exact 1D search on the grid, is stored as a certificate with stand-alone
  checkers. Includes a 1D phase diagram of the first-level gaps I_3, I_4, I_5 at kappa = 100 and the tongues above
  them (numerical classification, exact 1D searches).
